  "_comment": "A pontoon start straight that heaves with the swell, docks with crates and crane loads swinging over the quay, a hump over the old pier, off-camber dock turns, a banked climb onto the high pier bridge over the start straight, a banked hairpin round the lighthouse, a banked sweep down to the water and the dive: the road drops under the west quay and you drive along the harbour floor before climbing out. The drawbridge along the south quay lowers on a timer, the warehouse doors open for a while when someone hits the switch on the quay, and the tide floods the west docks from lap 2.",
